#Problem APEX 5.1.28

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Antiderivatives (with trigonometric functions))
## KEYWORDS(indefinite integral)
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.1')
## Problem1('28')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric')->flags->set(tolerance => 0.01, tolType => "absolute");

$a  = random(2, 10, 1) * random(-1, 1, 2);
$a1 = $a + 1;
$f  = Formula("-cos(x) + $a1");

BEGIN_PGML
Find the function [`f(x)`] described by the given
initial value problem.
[```
  f'(x) = \sin x, \qquad f(0) = [$a].
```]

[`f(x) =`] [____]{$f}{30}.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
[```  f(x) = \int \sin x \, dx = -\cos x + C.
```] 

We find the constant [`C`] by setting [`f(0) = [$a]`].
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

[``f(x) = \int \sin x \, dx = -\cos x + C.``]

We find the constant [`C`] by setting [`f(0) = [$a]`].

[`` -\cos(0) + C = [$a] \;\Rightarrow\; -1 + C = [$a]
  \;\Rightarrow\; C = [$a1].``]
  
Thus, [`f(x) = -\cos x + [$a1]`].

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    

